WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.500
A giant, monstrous, crab-like claw closes
around the throat of an unimaginably huge

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.260
eel-like beast.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.679
The beast’s terrible, writhing tentacles
wrap around and latch onto the immense crustacean,

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:18.820
and then the high-intensity beams of gamma
radiation start flying.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.810
All the while, legions of skinless centaurs
swim in the waters around them, relishing

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.039
the violence.

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:33.430
And in the middle, a lone boat, the SCPS Mither,
manned by a team of Mobile Task Force operatives,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.570
does all it can just to survive.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:41.140
There are those who consider outer space to
be the ultimate achievement in exploration,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.200
the one place that explorers have yet to chart
and understand.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.570
However, some of the murkiest mysteries in
the universe are on our own planet, deep down

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.710
at the bottom of the ocean.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:59.140
Ninety-five percent of the deep ocean remains
completely unexplored, and the little glimpses

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.289
we have gotten paint a picture of something
truly alien.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:10.220
Giant squids, organisms that can breathe nitrogen,
luminescent predatory fish, and sharks as

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.940
old as the earth itself.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:18.140
Even the SCP Foundation is still struggling
to fully grasp the depths of the ocean and

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.560
the strange beings that dwell there.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:29.240
One of the most unusual aquatic findings in
the history of the Foundation is that of SCP-3700.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:36.860
SCP-3700 refers to a circular area in the
North Sea with a diameter of 800 km.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:42.350
The waters there are abnormally deep for the
region, with the sea floor resting at 5 km

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.009
beneath the ocean's surface.

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:54.710
There are two entities present in the waters
of SCP-3700, designated SCP-3700-1 and SCP-3700-2.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:02:00.289
Interactions between these two entities are
responsible for anomalous changes to the meteorological

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:04.340
and geological conditions in the area.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:12.620
SCP-3700-1 and SCP-3700-2 always interact
on the Spring and Fall equinoxes of any given

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.500
year, but they will also engage one another
throughout the year, seemingly at random.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:24.510
But what, exactly, are SCP-3700-1 and 3700-2?

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.720
Aside from terrifying creatures of the deep.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:34.530
SCP-3700-1 is an arthropod bearing an aesthetic
resemblance to the European lobster, only

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.840
much, much bigger, measuring six km in length.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:44.120
The creature is green, with a mix of blue,
yellow, pink, and red markings across the

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.440
top of its exoskeleton that bear the appearance
of a woman's face.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:54.819
It has six prehensile limbs, four of which
terminate in claws, and eight legs.

00:02:54.819 --> 00:03:00.330
The entity's four eyes are compound and orange,
attached to stalks.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:04.659
Anyone who gets close enough to observe the
creature's carapace in detail will notice

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:11.360
scars, cracks, and small holes, indicating
years and years of damage.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:16.810
SCP-3700-1 has several anomalous qualities
in addition to its size.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.040
In a fight, it is able to strike with its
appendages and produce cavitation bubbles

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.019
with a force greater than several tons of
dynamite.

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:30.650
Two of the entity's eyes are capable of blasting
concentrated gamma radiation at a chosen target.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.010
The creature has the ability to impact the
weather around it, dispersing storms that

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:41.010
impede its ability to move with ease, and
can reach speeds of up to 100 km/hour.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:47.750
In spite of its immense power, SCP-3700-1
is not aggressive and tends to ignore beings

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:52.790
in its vicinity other than SCP-3700-2.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:04:02.560
Speaking of SCP-3700-2, it is a 32 km long
entity resembling a pelican eel in all aspects

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:10.060
except for its massive size, and the 13 appendages
that encircle the middle section of its body.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:15.560
These appendages, which tuck inside its body
when not in use, are similar to the tentacles

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.269
of an octopus, complete with suckers.

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:24.419
The majority of the entity's body consists
of a sinewy tail, terminating in a sharp point.

00:04:24.419 --> 00:04:28.479
When its mouth is open, it is an estimated
3 km deep.

00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:33.870
Its flesh is black, and it has white, purple,
and red bioluminescent lines in the shape

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.160
of a man's face on either side of its torso.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.860
SCP-3700-2's anomalous properties include
the ability to invoke storms with the severity

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:49.320
of category 5 hurricanes,and the ability to
produce whirlpools that draw in any vessel

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.410
within 150m so that it can rip them apart.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:59.820
It is also able to produce high-energy soundwaves
as well as blue fire, which it emits from

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.820
its esophagus.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:06.650
When the two entities interact, it results
in an epic struggle as each being attempts

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.620
to destroy or subdue the other.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:14.060
When one is victorious, immediate changes
to the area follow.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:20.630
When SCP-3700-1 wins, the storms and harsh
weather in the area will immediately calm,

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.130
and an era of fertility and abundance will
begin.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:29.780
The reproductive rates of fauna in the ocean
and on the islands nearby increase threefold,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.240
and the crop yield doubles.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.220
The ocean itself becomes increasingly active,
and the erosion rates of the archipelago's

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.880
shores increase fivefold.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:47.220
When SCP-3700-2 wins, however, the weather
conditions become dangerous, with raging hurricanes,

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:52.220
rapidly fluctuating temperatures, and constantly
changing storm fronts that cause destruction

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.150
of buildings and loss of life.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:06:01.730
Naturally, this renders any ocean travel in
the area extremely difficult or even impossible.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:06.990
Aquatic food sources are driven away by harsh
conditions, and livestock are killed by exposure

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.810
and disease.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:14.730
Crops are unable to thrive in the high winds,
waterlogged soil, and lack of sunlight.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:22.130
All the while, SCP-3700-2 swims throughout
the area, preying on unsuspecting ships and

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:29.790
menacing the coastline until SCP-3700-1 manifests
to challenge it again.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:37.979
SCP-3700-2 will also regurgitate instances
of SCP-3456, though how or why this is possible

00:06:37.979 --> 00:06:39.550
is unknown.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:46.450
For those unfamiliar with SCP-3456, they are
a group of hairless, three-toed horse-like

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:51.639
creatures with thick, translucent skin and
human torsos fused to their backs.

00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:57.389
They are most frequently seen near sites of
war, terrorist attacks, and devastating natural

00:06:57.389 --> 00:06:58.889
disasters.

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:02.879
Direct observation of one of these entities
will draw their attention to the observer,

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:07.150
who the entity will then stalk and capture
before disappearing.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:13.430
Due to their enormous size and ability to
anomalously manifest in their home waters,

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:18.340
SCP-3700-1 and 2 cannot be contained at a
Foundation site.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:24.009
Instead, their containment is handled by Foundation
Naval Task Force Delta-7, "Northern Storm,"

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:30.580
who patrol the area in a combination of refurbished
battleships, destroyers, cruisers, and support

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:31.580
craft.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:36.590
Additionally, measures have been taken to
suppress information about SCP-3700 among

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.760
the general population.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:43.259
Details about the unusual depth of the waters
there have been stricken from public texts

00:07:43.259 --> 00:07:46.039
and scientific publications.

00:07:46.039 --> 00:07:52.669
SCP-3700-1 has been implanted with Donovan
holoprojectors, which disguise it as a pod

00:07:52.669 --> 00:07:54.419
of humpback whales.

00:07:54.419 --> 00:08:03.229
If SCP-3700-1 encounters SCP-3700-2, Delta-7
may engage Protocol "Winter Maelstrom."

00:08:03.229 --> 00:08:10.830
This consists of destroyers deploying harpoon-based
anchors into SCP-3700-2's head, to hold it

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.319
in one location.

00:08:12.319 --> 00:08:18.930
Next, the vessels work together to target
the entity until SCP-3700-1 is able to subdue

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.930
it.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:26.509
If this does not prove effective, and SCP-3700-2
cannot be contained, then the task force will

00:08:26.509 --> 00:08:28.080
implement Protocol Tumult.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:32.610
At this point, naval and civilian crafts in
the area must be evacuated.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:37.450
Trade and ferry routes to the archipelagos
must be rerouted for at least six months.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:44.180
There will be constant aerial and naval engagement
with SCP-3700-2, and constant monitoring for

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.080
the reappearance of SCP-3700-1.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:55.890
The behavior of SCP-3700-1 and SCP-3700-2
is largely very predictable, with one notable

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:56.900
exception.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:04.100
On March 20, 2017, a pair of SCP Foundation-owned
battleships known as the Mither and the Teran

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:09.529
arrived at a point between the Orkney, Shetland,
and Faroe Archipelagos in the North Sea.

00:09:09.529 --> 00:09:13.840
They were accompanied by the usual fleet of
Delta-7 ships.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.800
Approximately 600 meters away from the ships'
anchor points, the water began to emit intense,

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.029
bright rays of light for a duration of three
minutes.

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:28.180
At this point, SCP-3700-1 appeared, visible
through the surface of the water.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:31.530
Delta-7 withdrew their anchors, speeding toward
the entity.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:36.269
As the ships caught up to the entity, it raised
two of its claws into the air, clicking them

00:09:36.269 --> 00:09:38.490
together in a friendly greeting.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:43.690
The Delta-7 ships followed the entity along
its usual swimming path for 30 minutes, and

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.300
during this time, all was peaceful.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.079
But this peace didn't endure for long.

00:09:49.079 --> 00:09:55.550
The tide began to change, literally, as large
black wall clouds formed overhead, the winds

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:58.610
picked up, and the waves churned violently.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:05.580
In response, SCP-3700-1 raised its claws overhead,
waving them in a circular motion and parting

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.310
the clouds above it and Delta-7.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:12.870
But this effort took a lot out of the creature,
and after thirty seconds, its antenna began

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.160
to droop, and it lowered its claws.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:21.070
Still, the hole in the clouds remained, allowing
a spot of sunshine to break through and beam

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:23.670
down on the Foundation vessels.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:30.090
600 meters ahead, the ocean waters began to
rage and froth, spraying foam and surf into

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.800
the air.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:36.829
SCP-3700-2 burst from beneath the surface,
its head pointed upward.

00:10:36.829 --> 00:10:41.980
It continued to rise until the tops of its
tentacles could be seen above the water, then

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:46.269
stopped to bend its torso and turn its head
horizontally.

00:10:46.269 --> 00:10:51.360
Its jaw unhinged, exposing rows upon rows
of serrated teeth.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:56.300
The beast let loose a mighty roar, accompanied
by a stream of blue flame.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:02.820
At the sight of its rival, SCP-3700-1 dove
beneath the surface, disappearing from view.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:08.040
The SCPS Mither ordered the rest of the vessels
to engage "Protocol Winter Maelstrom."

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:14.210
Delta-7 scattered out from SCP-3700-1's point
of submersion, and all thirteen destroyers

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:20.620
fired their harpoons at SCP-3700-2, embedding
themselves in the entity's head.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:25.940
Naturally, this enraged the creature, and
it began to roar and wail, spinning its lower

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:29.420
body vigorously enough to generate a whirlpool.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:34.000
The cruisers opened fire with a combination
of L-cannons and conventional weaponry in

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:39.140
order to distract the entity as the destroyers
pulled their harpoon lines taut, dragging

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:41.420
its head in a continuous circle.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:46.170
While this was taking place, the battleships
got into position and prepared to fire on

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.139
the Mither's mark.

00:11:48.139 --> 00:11:49.440
3...2...1...

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.740
FIRE!

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:57.240
The first broadside barrage collided with
SCP-3700-2, and it grunted in pain, thrashing

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:04.500
back and forth, before opening its mouth and
spewing an instance of SCP-3456 into the water.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:10.200
As soon as it hit the water, the equine monster
began to cut through the water at a pace of

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:15.760
50 km/hour, making its way toward the destroyers,
particularly the SCPS Selkie.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.839
The Selkie attempted to retarget its weapons
and prevent the creature from reaching it,

00:12:19.839 --> 00:12:23.199
but the monster moved too quickly for the
Selkie to adjust.

00:12:23.199 --> 00:12:27.310
The Selkie was lifted out of the water by
the creature as crew members desperately clung

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.560
to the railing and their weaponry.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.790
As the crew cowered and tried to fend off
the creature, it reached for them, trying

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.330
to pull them from the ship.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:41.540
While the Selkie was occupied, SCP-3700-2
was able to attack again, blasting another

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.110
ship with a stream of blue fire.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:51.750
A loud CRACK rang out across the sea as the
Selkie dropped back into the water, the SCP-3456

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.410
instance shrieking in pain.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:58.880
SCP-3700-1 burst through the surface of the
water, striking the creature with its club-like

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.070
limbs, each blow emitting another loud crack.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:07.020
The third blow tore the instance in half,
sending its human torso careening through

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:10.420
the air and past the SCPS Mither.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:15.370
Freed from its attack, the Selkie moved full
steam ahead, pulling the harpoon line tight

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:20.190
again and dragging SCP-3700-2 out of its path.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:24.290
Several Selkie crew members were thrown overboard
during the struggle, and as they struggled

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:29.630
to keep their heads above water, SCP-3700-1
scooped them from the water, placing them

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:33.029
onto the deck of a nearby destroyer and out
of harm's way.

00:13:33.029 --> 00:13:39.490
With the crew members rescued, SC-3700-1 set
its sights on its enemy, swimming toward the

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:44.019
edge of the whirlpool and emitting a luminescent
glow from two of its eyes.

00:13:44.019 --> 00:13:50.140
The constant barrage of cannon fire on SCP-3700-2
was beginning to take its toll, and the Mither

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:54.329
ordered the fleet to "Brace for the killing
blow!"

00:13:54.329 --> 00:14:00.699
As if responding to the Mither's call, SCP-3700-1
shot several concentrated blasts of gamma

00:14:00.699 --> 00:14:07.050
radiation at its foe, leaving large holes
in the creature in their wake.

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:12.589
SCP-3700-2 screamed, flailing so hard that
it snapped the harpoon lines and created waves

00:14:12.589 --> 00:14:15.240
large enough to push the vessels backward.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:23.210
With this newfound freedom, SCP-3700-2 impaled
SCP-3700-1 through the midsection with the

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:28.720
barbed tip of its tail, lifting it up and
out of the water with the force of the blow.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:34.339
SCP-3700-1 desperately tried to free itself,
attacking the tail with its club-like limbs,

00:14:34.339 --> 00:14:39.880
but the fight was in vain, and after a moment,
all movement stopped.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:46.230
SCP-3700-1 was, for at least the duration
of this manifestation, dead.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:51.710
SCP-3700-2 tossed the corpse into the wair,
flinging it past Delta-7 where it crashed

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:55.519
into the water and sank down into the depths
below.

00:14:55.519 --> 00:14:58.889
At this point, Delta-7 was ordered to initiate
Protocol Tumult.

00:14:58.889 --> 00:15:05.470
The Delta-7 vessels turned away from SCP-3700-2,
preparing to evacuate the area.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:10.779
One of the ships, the SCPS Stronsay Beast,
slowed behind the rest of the fleet, emitting

00:15:10.779 --> 00:15:14.570
concerning amounts of smoke, before coming
to a stop.

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:21.380
Meanwhile, the enraged and emboldened SCP-3700-2
expanded the size of its whirlpool, setting

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:25.449
its sights on the retreating ships and the
weakened Stronsay Beast.

00:15:25.449 --> 00:15:30.319
The ship tried to flee, but the engines were
completely shot and would not respond.

00:15:30.319 --> 00:15:36.410
The ship was caught in the whirlpool and pulled
against its will toward SCP-3700-2.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:41.440
As the crew looked on in helpless dread, a
tentacle rose from the deep, wrapping around

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.149
the vessel and dragging it toward the entity's
gaping maw.

00:15:46.149 --> 00:15:52.060
Suddenly, SCP-3700-1 exploded from beneath
the surface of the water, leaping between

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:58.160
the ship and SCP-3700-2, cutting the tentacle
in half and freeing the Stronsay Beast from

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.420
its grip.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:06.399
SCP-3700-2 shrieked, before closing its jaws
and biting down on SCP-3700-1.

00:16:06.399 --> 00:16:12.790
It retaliated, emitting bright flashes of
light and doing enough damage to stop SCP-3700-2

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.510
from continuing to produce its whirlpool.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:21.360
Another tentacle emerged from the water, pulling
at SCP-3700-1's legs and ripping them from

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:29.290
its body, but SCP-3700-1 returned the assault
in kind, bludgeoning SCP-3700-2 with its club-like

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.810
limbs from inside of its mouth.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:38.440
All at once, SCP-3700-2's lower jaw was torn
out of place, dropping into the water with

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:42.490
SCP-3700-1 still inside.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:47.790
SCP-3700-2 thrashed futilely, growing steadily
weaker and weaker.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:51.440
It released one more stream of fire, before
collapsing.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.730
Delta-7 paused their retreat, watching the
scene for any sign of a winner, but after

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:59.209
five minutes, neither entity had moved.

00:16:59.209 --> 00:17:03.740
Delta-7 returned to the site of the battle
to investigate, and saw that neither entity

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.780
was moving, and both appeared to be deceased.

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:13.039
Shortly after Delta-7 reached the area, both
entities disappeared, leaving a single round

00:17:13.039 --> 00:17:19.970
unidentified object that sank below the surface
where SCP-3700-1 had just been.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:25.350
The wall clouds overhead dispersed, leaving
standard cumulonimbus clouds in their place.

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:27.589
The waters themselves remained choppy.

00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:32.049
Unsure of how to proceed, the SCPS Mither
sent a radio transmission to Command.

00:17:32.049 --> 00:17:33.780
"This is Delta-7 to Command."

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.700
"We read you Delta-7."

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:36.700
Command replied.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.500
"We have a bit of a situation."

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.950
"Go ahead, Delta-7."

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:45.270
"SCP-3700-1 and 2 are both down."

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:49.130
Command was silent for ten seconds, utterly
baffled by the information.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.970
"Please repeat Delta-7."

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:57.330
Again, the Mither said, "SCP-3700-1 and 2
are both down."

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.190
Command ordered the Mither to "stand by."

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:05.179
Three minutes of radio silence later, communication
resumed as they asked: "Are either entities'

00:18:05.179 --> 00:18:06.429
effects active?"

00:18:06.429 --> 00:18:07.890
"Negative command."

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.480
"Is there any trace of either entity?"

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.480
"Also negative."

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.350
"It appears the anomaly has been neutralized.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:19.190
Dela-7 is to return to base for debrief following
any recovery efforts."

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:24.799
With their next steps clear, Delta-7 attached
the Stronsay Beast to several tug boats, preparing

00:18:24.799 --> 00:18:26.580
to pull the vessel to safety.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.760
But there were more surprises waiting.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:34.940
The SCPS Mither began picking up unusual levels
of gamma radiation, as well as a sonar contact

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.260
at a depth of 3 km.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:42.050
They called command, requesting permission
to deploy submersibles for exploration purposes.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:45.960
One minute of silence followed, as the command
arrived at a decision.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.590
"Request denied.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.190
Return to base for debriefing."

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:54.750
And so, Delta-7 began to evacuate the area
once more, steaming in the opposite direction

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:55.900
of the battle.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:01.179
Over the next five minutes, CCTV cameras on
the vessels picked up an unusual sight.

00:19:01.179 --> 00:19:06.610
As the gamma radiation levels continued to
increase, the ocean turbulence also worsened,

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.980
tossing smaller vessels and nearly causing
them to capsize.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:16.230
Then, all of a sudden, the waters stilled,
and four large, yellow orbs appeared below

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:20.470
the surface, approximately 300m from Delta-7.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:23.070
They lingered there for two minutes before
vanishing.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:29.570
Afterward, a new sonar contact was detected,
5k km deep, directly beneath the task force.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:33.690
"Command, we've lost the signal from the previous
contact and are no longer detecting gamma

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.299
radiation.

00:19:35.299 --> 00:19:38.760
We're detecting a new contact, 5 km deep,
large, and metallic."

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.600
After further deliberation, Command responded:

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:45.690
"Delta-7, you are authorized to deploy submersibles
for exploration purposes.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:52.590
Be advised, should SCP-3700-2 manifest, exploration
teams are to be considered lost, and you are

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:54.240
to return to base."

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:58.510
The consequences of this incident, as well
as what else might be lurking down in the

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:02.280
depths beneath SCP-3700, are still unknown.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:09.710
Now go check out “SCP-169 - Leviathan”
and “SCP-057-IT - Under the Sea!”

